  "body": "Found during the review of PR #860 (#33, C unwind), where the lathe post got this cap.\n\n**What happens:** `assets/posts/fanuc.cps` (about lines 109-114) and `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps` (about line 287) write a C word on a combined linear + rotary move at the operation's F, with no check against the rotary rate the machine file states. A short linear move with a large C change can therefore command the rotary far faster than its stated maximum.\n\n**What #860 does for the lathe post:** `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps` (`liveMove`) caps F on every C block so that the linear part does not exceed the machine's stated linear feed and the C part does not exceed its stated C rate (deg/min; the rotary `speeds` are passed to the script by `crates/post/src/post/machine.rs`), with zero-length guards. Where the machine file states no C rate, C is uncapped by data.\n\n**Expected:** every post that writes a rotary word on a combined move applies the same rule from the same machine data (one helper, not a copy per post), or refuses by name where it cannot. Check the other dialects that can emit A/B/C on a combined move as well (tormach.cps for the microARC A, the 5-axis posts).\n\n**Open question for the fix:** how each control reads F on a combined move (linear feed with the rotary carried along, a combined rate, or inverse time G93) - the cap must match the feed mode the post declares; cite the control's public documentation per dialect.\n\nDone means: no posted block can command a rotary above its stated rate or a linear axis above the stated feed; pinned per dialect by a test that reads every posted block back; existing goldens move only where a block was over the limit, each listed.\n\nSafety floor (posted G-code): effort high, high-tier review.\n",
